[doc title="CX Language Guide" author="Erik" version="0.8.0"

  [h1 CX Language Guide]

  [p CX is a [strong structured] markup language with [em clean] bracket
  syntax. It exports to XML, JSON, YAML, and TOML.]

  [h2 Quick Start]

  [p Install and build:]

  [pre [code lang=bash [#
git clone https://github.com/cx-home/cx
make build              # builds libcx + every binding
make promote-cli        # install the cx CLI
#]]]

  [p Then try [code cx --help] to see all options.]

  [h2 Core Concepts]

  [h3 Inline Formatting]

  [p Supports [strong bold], [em italic], [strong [em bold italic]],
  [del strikethrough], [sub subscript], [sup superscript], [u underline],
  and [code inline code].]

  [h3 Lists]

  [ul
    [li Clean bracket syntax]
    [li Typed attributes on any element — sized types like ::u16 / ::f64]
    [li Multiple output formats]
    [li Boolean attributes: tls=true / debug=false]
  ]

  [h3 Links]

  [p See the [a href="https://cxhome.org/docs" full documentation] for details.]

  [h3 Tables]

  [formats [table[format::string input::bool output::bool]]
    CX   true true
    XML  true true
    JSON true true
    YAML true true
    TOML true true
  ]

